ess><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OGUCHI MINORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WADA KUNIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJITA, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJIWARA, TOSHIHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HONMA, HIDEHITO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGUCHI, MINORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WADA, KUNIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Amine derivatives represented by general formula (I) or pharmacologically acceptable salts thereof, which are useful as therapeutic and/or preventive agents for diabetes, hyperlipemia, arteriosclerosis, cancers, and so on: wherein R1 is optionally substituted carbamoyl or the like; R2 is hydrogen or the like; R3 is C1-C10 alkyl or the like; W1, W2 and W3 are each independently a single bond or C1-C8 alkylene; X, Y and Q are each sulfur or the like; Z is =CH- or the like; Ar is a benzene ring or the like; and L is hydrogen or the like.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention se rapporte à des dérivés amine représentés de formule générale (I) ou à un sel pharmaceutiquement acceptable de ces dérivés, qui s'avèrent utiles en tant qu'agents thérapeutiques et/ou préventifs du diabète, de l'hyperlipidémie, de l'artériosclérose, du cancer, etc. Dans la formule (I), R1 est carbamoyle éventuellement substitué ou analogue; R2 est hydrogène ou analogue; R3 est alkyle C1-C10 ou analogue; W1, W2 et W3 sont chacun indépendamment une liaison simple ou un alkylène C1-C8; X, Y et Q sont chacun soufre ou analogue; Z est =CH- ou analogue; Ar est un noyau benzène ou analogue; et L est hydrogène ou analogue.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>